{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "For U3 (Mail TLS/SSL), use the existing java-mail-properties attribute with a util:properties bean, avoiding changes to the Mail sink's core API",
    "For U7 (compression), implement a reusable transformer/processor module rather than embedding compression logic in individual sinks/sources, following Spring XD module conventions",
    "For U8 (Rabbit compression), use Spring AMQP's native compression support (RabbitMQ message compression mode) and expose it as module options",
    "For U6 (YML manifest), introduce a separate deployment-manifest.yml loaded at stream deployment time so it can be shared across multiple stream definitions",
    "For U5 (upgrade), follow Spring XD's existing BOM-based dependency management pattern; bump parent spring-boot.version to 1.2.0.RELEASE first, then propagate transitive upgrades",
    "For U2 (Snappy/codec), expose codec as a configurable option on the hdfs-dataset sink, defaulting to current behavior (snappy on) for backward compatibility",
    "For U4 (partitionResultsTimeout), expose the attribute through the job metadata XML schema and the REST API representation without changing the underlying Spring Batch configuration",
    "Apply consistent unit + integration test coverage for each user story using existing JUnit/Spring Test infrastructure"
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "One work day equals 8 productive hours for a single developer performing all the work",
    "The Spring XD codebase, build environment (Maven), CI pipeline, and a representative test runtime are already available to the developer",
    "U1 is interpreted as standing up the benchmark harness and producing comparison stats (not only running an existing one); benchmark environment is treated as pre-provisioned",
    "U5's upgrade assumes the dependency versions listed in the story are accepted as-is and no further research on newer patch versions is required",
    "Integration testing for each story is counted in the per-story effort; the dedicated integration test activity covers end-to-end cross-module validation after all stories are implemented",
    "Documentation updates cover the public wiki pages, module option Javadocs, and release notes; no new marketing material is produced",
    "No major architectural refactoring is implied beyond what is necessary to deliver the listed user stories",
    "No dedicated security review, legal review, or production rollout/superwatch activity is included"
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A1",
      "activity_name": "Requirements analysis and design",
      "activity_description": "Review all eight user stories, clarify scope, draft high-level design notes (module options, APIs, configuration files), and identify cross-cutting impacts (e.g., effect of Spring Boot upgrade on U6 manifest loader).",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2",
      "activity_name": "U1 - Sqoop vs jdbchdfs benchmark",
      "activity_description": "Set up a reproducible benchmark job for Sqoop import and for the jdbchdfs batch job on a representative dataset, capture throughput/latency/resource stats, and document the comparison results for the QA team.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3",
      "activity_name": "U2 - Disable Snappy / configurable Avro codec for hdfs-dataset sink",
      "activity_description": "Add a codec option to the hdfs-dataset sink (e.g., snappy, deflate, none, custom) and wire it to the Avro writer configuration; preserve existing default behavior; add unit tests for the new option.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4",
      "activity_name": "U3 - TLS/SSL support for Mail sink",
      "activity_description": "Allow the Mail sink to honor JavaMail SSL/TLS properties supplied via a util:properties bean (java-mail-properties attribute). Cover both IMAP and SMTP secured variants, including the imaps/smtps protocol selection. Add tests against a mock secured mail server.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5",
      "activity_name": "U4 - Expose partitionResultsTimeout as job metadata",
      "activity_description": "Surface the partitionResultsTimeout Spring Batch property through the job metadata XML schema and the XD job/rest representation for the three OOTB jobs (and any other importing jobs). Add unit and integration tests for the metadata lookup.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6",
      "activity_name": "U5 - Spring Boot 1.2.0 RELEASE and dependency upgrade",
      "activity_description": "Bump the parent spring-boot.version to 1.2.0.RELEASE and update the ~35 listed dependency versions (activemq, aspectj, hibernate, hikaricp, jackson, jetty, spring, spring-batch, spring-data, tomcat, etc.). Resolve breaking API changes, fix compilation, re-run the full test suite, and adjust any deprecated API usages.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7",
      "activity_name": "U6 - Separate YML for deployment manifest properties",
      "activity_description": "Introduce a deployment-manifest.yml file that holds shared deployment manifest properties; refactor stream deployment to load from this file so the same manifest is not duplicated in every stream definition. Add parser/loader tests and sample YML.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8",
      "activity_name": "U7 - Message compression modules (gzip, zip)",
      "activity_description": "Implement compression and decompression processor modules (gzip and zip) usable in any stream. Validate with round-trip tests, stream compatibility checks, and performance smoke tests to confirm the intended throughput influence.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A9",
      "activity_name": "U8 - Rabbit source/sink compression options",
      "activity_description": "Add compression options to the Rabbit source and sink modules (using Spring AMQP's compression support) with a codec choice and on/off toggle. Verify with an end-to-end test that compressed and uncompressed payloads are correctly produced and consumed.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A10",
      "activity_name": "Cross-module integration testing",
      "activity_description": "Run an end-to-end integration test pass covering: upgraded Spring Boot stack (A6), TLS mail sink (A4), compression transformers (A8) composed with the Rabbit modules (A9), and the new deployment manifest YML (A7). Fix any regressions surfaced.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A11",
      "activity_name": "Documentation and wiki updates",
      "activity_description": "Update the public wiki/module reference pages for: new mail sink TLS example, codec option on hdfs-dataset, compression processor modules, Rabbit source/sink compression options, partitionResultsTimeout metadata, and the deployment-manifest YML usage. Draft release notes summarizing the changes.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A12",
      "activity_name": "Build, packaging, and release preparation",
      "activity_description": "Run a full clean build with the new dependency versions, generate updated distribution artifacts, verify module registration/manifests, and tag/prepare a release candidate build for the XD admin team.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 40
  }
}
```

